# Line endings.
#
# The DXF writer emits LF and the golden files in fixtures/ are byte-compared,
# so git must never rewrite their line endings. Without this, a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true by default) turns every golden file into CRLF
# and the whole golden-file suite fails there — and re-approving with
# UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 on Windows would commit CRLF files that then break everyone
# else.

# Normalise text files to LF in the repository and in the working tree, so the
# repo behaves the same on every machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden files are compared byte for byte: git must leave them exactly alone.
*.dxf -text

# Genuinely binary assets.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.wasm binary
